Z||000002||Alex4mula||03-14-2001||08:29 AM||||245-45 should not stick out at all. I have 235-40-17 in the rear & looks perfect. I don't think 10mm more will do anything substantial.||||reg||1
Z||000003||KRMFiero||03-14-2001||08:30 AM||||I am 95% sure the tires will fit on the back,  shock type struts i think you mean coil overs. I dont think those tires will stick out, or i dont think they will stick out much depending what the offset of your Rims are, i am not any type of expert on this so hopefully someone will post something<P>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000004||Philphine||03-14-2001||09:24 AM||||don't know how wide your wheel is. i have 255/50-16 on the rear of my '87 on 7.5" wheels and they don't stick out. the wheel wells look really full though and you need coilovers. i probaly won't do it again. i may go with the size you're trying or go back to the same size all around. probaly 225/45 or50-16.||||reg||1
